afk: prompt wording only — mention jj alongside git in the hardcoded
prompts (system-prompt, orchestrate-notice, plan-mode-active,
commit-message-system).

Motivation: this distribution mandates jj (profile/rules/jj-basics.md),
but omp's built-in prompts speak raw git (`git status`, branch talk,
commit instructions). Agents follow the nearest instruction, so the
built-ins must at least name the jj equivalents (`jj st`,
`jj describe`) instead of contradicting the rule files.

What must survive a rebase:
- No behavior change, prose only. If upstream rewrote these prompt
  files, re-apply the intent (jj named wherever git subcommands are
  prescribed) rather than the exact wording. (18.0.11 compressed all
  four prompts; the same four spots were re-worded in place.)

